course: dictionary
lesson: 12140
title: Communicative: talking and sharing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A communicative person is willing and happy to talk and share information with other people. The word comes from communicate, which means to pass on ideas or news. «Maya is very communicative, and she tells everyone about her day.» Maya likes talking and sharing, so communicative means willing to talk.
explain: The word can also describe things to do with communication. In language lessons, a communicative approach means learning by talking in real situations, such as ordering food or asking the way. «Our teacher uses a communicative approach, so we practise speaking French every day.» Here communicative describes the way the lessons are taught.
explain: Reports often use this word about a child. «Sam is not very communicative in class, but he writes wonderful stories.» This tells you Sam is quiet and does not share his ideas out loud much. Not very communicative is a polite way of saying someone is quiet or shy about talking.
fact: Communicative means willing and happy to talk and share information with others.
fact: Communicative also means to do with communication, such as communicative skills.
fact: The word comes from communicate, which means to pass on ideas, news or feelings.
fact: «Not very communicative» means someone is quiet and does not talk much.
fact: A communicative approach to learning a language means learning by talking in real situations.
exercise: «Maya is very communicative and tells everyone about her day.» What does communicative mean here? | *Willing and happy to talk and share ideas | Very loud and noisy | Shy and always alone | Good at running fast
exercise: «Sam is not very communicative in class.» What does this suggest about Sam? | He is always the first to answer every question | He cannot read or write | He talks all the time and never stops | *He is quiet and does not share his ideas out loud much
exercise: «Our teacher uses a communicative approach, so we practise speaking French every day.» Find and copy one word that is about communication. | *communicative | practise | teacher | approach
test: «Ben is so communicative that he chats to the new children on their first day.» What does communicative mean? | *Happy to talk and share with others | Angry and loud | Hard to hear | Good at drawing
test: Which sentence uses communicative to mean to do with communication? | The dog was very communicative and slept all day | My shoes are communicative and bright | *Learning French through real conversations is a communicative way to learn | He is the most communicative runner in the race
exam: Mia's report says, «She is not very communicative yet, but she is improving.» What does the report mean? | Mia has stopped going to school | *Mia is still learning to talk and share her ideas with others | Mia is the best at talking in the whole class | Mia talks far too much in every lesson
